**What was built.** `lean/MOSPFormalization/DegreeBound/SPReduction.lean` defines the three series-parallel operations as an inductive step relation that carries its vertex, their reflexive-transitive closure, "reduced" and "basic", and proves 69 theorems with no `sorry` and no `axiom`. R1 through R5 of the plan are all proved. The commutation lemma R3 replaces the paper's appeal to Kneis et al.'s confluence, and its lift R4 takes the hypothesis that the deleted set lies in the support of the reduct, which is exactly what item 08 will supply. The file compiled clean on its first full attempt.

**Checked before stated.** The brute-force script re-ran R3 on every graph to 9 vertices in the form the proof produces, recording which case and which constructor fires. The counts match item 02's to the triple. The finset form, the R4 replay along random maximal reductions, R5 with a random disjoint graph, and step existence were checked for the first time. Zero violations.

